LITERATURE REVIEW
2.0.	 Introduction
 This section seeks to present an overview of different research works on the application of artificial intelligence (AI) in mental health care, particularly on cognitive behavioral therapy (CBT). It seeks to discuss concepts, technologies, and research findings on AI in mental health care. By combining different views from psychology, AI, and human interaction with technology, this section seeks to offer a comprehensive assessment of the ability of AI-assisted therapies and their limitations in addressing different mental health issues facing the world. With increasing demand for psychological therapies and a significant shortage of mental health professionals, there is an urgent need to develop cost-effective and efficient solutions (World Health Organization, 2022). AI tools have shown significant potential in addressing this problem. With AI tools, when integrated with CBT, it seeks to offer a combination of traditional psychological therapies and new technologies. This chapter starts by introducing concepts in psychological therapies before proceeding to discuss AI-assisted therapies.
2.1.  	Psychological Therapy
Psychological therapy is defined as a broad group of organized interventions intended to alleviate emotional pain, change undesirable behavior, and improve mental well-being (National Institute of Mental Health, 2023). Psychotherapy, guided by various theories and approaches, offers people a safe and comfortable environment to explore their ideas, emotions, and actions with the assistance of qualified mental health professionals (Cleveland Clinic, 2022). Not only does it make you feel better right away, but it also makes you emotionally stronger and more aware of yourself and your problems and how to solve them in a positive manner.
According to Beck (2011), therapy is a hands-on and cooperative process in which people can identify and change their bad thought processes and hence respond to events in their lives more positively. This method of doing things is helpful in dealing with anxiety disorders, depression, and mood swings because bad thoughts and actions are what cause and maintain mental anguish.
Psychotherapy is of various forms, such as individual therapy, group therapy, family therapy, and couples therapy, and so on. However, they have one main purpose in common: to encourage psychological growth and development through organized and meaningful interaction (Open Textbooks BC, 2021). 
2.2.1.	Types of Psychological Therapy
This section examines the primary therapy methods used in mental health treatment which people can access through both physical and digital platforms.  Different therapy methods use distinct theoretical frameworks to provide their unique approaches for treating mental health disorders.
Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT) is a common treatment. The therapy provides a structured treatment which requires less time than most other therapies. The system examines how three interconnected elements which include thoughts and feelings and actions create mutual effects. CBT treatment method operates on the premise that negative thought patterns lead to emotional difficulties and behavioral disorders. The CBT approach helps individuals identify their existing thought patterns evaluate their validity and select superior alternatives. The treatment program requires essential components which include self-monitoring activities and cognitive transformation and goal establishment and physical engagement. The structured nature of CBT allows for online implementation through chatbots and website systems which enable AI technology to function effectively. (National Institute of Mental Health, 2021).
Dialectical Behavior Therapy (DBT), an extension of CBT, incorporates acceptance-based strategies alongside cognitive restructuring. The treatment method provides special benefits to patients who experience emotional instability and self-destructive behavior and borderline personality disorder symptoms. The DBT program teaches essential abilities which include mindfulness practice and distress management and emotional control techniques. Selected DBT components have been converted into digital formats which allow their delivery through online platforms although AI systems still face difficulties with full system implementation (Verywell Health, 2023).
