3.9.3 	Ethical Considerations
Artificial intelligence systems used in therapeutic environments require special protection measures which need to be established through multiple ethical safeguards that will protect study participants while handling system operations. 
Informed Consent: The study participants receive complete information about the project objectives, data collection methods, and their ability to withdraw from the research at any moment before they begin the study or interact with the chatbot system. The chatbot system requires users to accept its terms before they can start their conversation which serves as the method for obtaining user consent. 
Confidentiality and Data Privacy: The system maintains complete confidentiality when it processes user information which includes their emotional reactions and mood assessments and their complete usage activity. The system processes all data as anonymous and stores it within protected databases that use encryption. The system only gathers personal identification details when users provide their explicit consent. Only research team members have the right to access the collected data. 
Use of Ethical AI: The chatbot is designed to prevent it from making diagnostic statements or therapeutic assessments. The platform provides users with CBT-based conversational support which helps them find professional treatment for their serious mental health requirements. The AI system contains disclaimers which define its operational scope during emergency situations that require predefined escalation procedures.



















