This project focused on the design and development of an AI therapist chatbot employing Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT) methodologies to assist mental wellness. The system was designed as a web-based application utilizing React.js/Next.js for the frontend, Node.js/Express.js for the backend, and MongoDB for data management. It combines crucial elements such as user registration and login, mood tracking, activity logging, and interactive chatbot sessions, allowing users to receive CBT-based coaching suited to their specific needs. The database structure was carefully developed to manage user information, session details, mood entries, activities, and chat histories, enabling the chatbot to retain context-aware interactions and give personalized responses. Extensive system testing, including unit testing, integration testing, and user acceptance testing, was undertaken to validate functionality, usability, and performance. The test findings revealed that the system functions reliably, correctly handles edge cases such as invalid inputs and session timeouts, and achieves the objectives established during the design phase.
5.2 	Conclusion
The development of this AI therapist chatbot revealed that an AI-driven system can serve as a useful tool for mental health support. The chatbot enables users to complete CBT activities while it evaluates their mood and activity patterns and it provides personalized interactions that use their past session data which creates an effective therapeutic process. The project demonstrated how proper database design and effective session handling and error management lead to building an effective system that users can operate without difficulty. The system demonstrates that AI-based chatbots can enhance traditional mental health treatment methods which improve access to care for patients who need support by delivering complete functional requirements and contextually relevant user interfaces.



5.3 	Recommendations
The design and construction and testing of the AI therapist chatbot together with user feedback documented in Appendix II lead to multiple recommendations which should be implemented for future system improvements.
The first recommendation was the need to enhance chatbot AI capabilities through the implementation of advanced natural language processing and sentiment analysis systems. The system will deliver better results because users requested quick answers which will improve their interaction with the system according to Appendix II.
It was also recommended that system needs to implement multiple languages because users from different linguistic backgrounds require it and international users will benefit from this development according to certain respondents.
There was also a recommendation for needs to establish advanced security and privacy measures which include email verification and data encryption and two-factor authentication for protecting confidential user data according to participant recommendations.
The system needs to implement features which will enable users to delete their sessions and work with mobile applications and connect with human therapists for situations that need expert assistance according to user feedback documented in Appendix II.
5.4.	 Limitations 
The testing process showed multiple limitations which emerged during the AI therapist chatbot evaluation after its successful building and testing process. The chatbot achieved an overall accuracy of roughly 69% which showed that most responses matched the context but some interactions failed to meet user needs. The existing natural language processing system and the current prompt configuration technique both show operational. 
The evaluation dataset contained limited data because it primarily used user feedback from Google Forms (Appendix II). A larger and more diverse sample size would provide a more comprehensive assessment of system performance and reliability. 
The system operates through CBT-based response frameworks because it fails to deliver complete mental health treatment. The system will struggle to address psychological emergencies that need human intervention and to manage intricate psychological assessments. 
Basic authentication methods received implementation, but full system security protection through end-to-end encryption and multi-factor authentication procedure implementation remained incomplete. The system operates as a web-based platform which provides limited access to customers who need dedicated mobile applications and offline functionality.
5.5.	Future Research 
The research in future studies should develop AI therapist chatbot systems that work better in real-world situations. The primary method involves using advanced Natural Language Processing systems which help users understand text better and stop them from making errors through the use of input. The system requires better techniques for detecting emotions and classifying purposes so it can handle emotions that people show through their behavior. 
Development of extensive user testing which includes various testing groups that have different backgrounds. The research action would provide better evidence about how the system works and its usability and treatment results which different age groups and cultural backgrounds experience. 
Supervised learning methods should be explored to enable continuous improvement of chatbot responses through analysis of anonymous user feedback. The system will reach better performance results when it uses this method for improving accuracy. 
The dedicated mobile application would need to turn the platform into its full potential because it would help analyze how people use the system during their daily life activities which leads to better understanding of user engagement and retention and treatment results.


